<blockquote class="uncited"><div>Why do I have to select the COM port twice? </div></blockquote>AFIK, this is something strange associated with Windows installing a driver per USB port.<br><br>Normally once a driver is installed on one port, Windows will automatically install it again onto a different product is plugged in, but in your case this doesn't seem to be happening.<br><br>You could try selecting the non-functioning port in the device manager and manually loading the driver files.<br><br><a href="https://www.opengd77.com/downloads/drivers/com_driver_files.zip" class="postlink">downloads/drivers/com_driver_files.zip</a><p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=50">VK3KYY</a> — Sun Jan 05, 2025 11:56 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
