		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=4736&amp;p=35006#p35006"><![CDATA[
Hi. First query.<br><br>I have a Baofeng DM1701 flashed with OpenGD77. My (Windows 10) PC has a number of USB ports. In one of them (call it "A"), I plug the radio and the PC says "Device not Recognised". Device Manager says "Unknown USB Device (Device Descriptor Request Failed)". I plug into another (call it "B") and W10 has no issues: it creates a new COM port.<br><br>The port A issue, I don't understand, but with respect to port B, if I then fire up the OpenGD77 CPS, and try to flash the codeplug, it makes me select a COM port. It's annoying, but fair enough. It then makes me select the COM port again, and from that point it works fine.<br><br>Why do I have to select the COM port twice? This is repeatable.<br><br>This had been working fine. The only thing I can think of that changed was that I installed the Retevis CPS and it may have changed the driver.<br> <br>I don't  an on using the Retevis software, so if any solution involves uninstalling it ... no big deal.<br><br>Thanks.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=7623">2E0UMK</a> — Sun Jan 05, 2025 9:51 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
